10. How do you change file permissions to allow only the owner to read and write? (CO1)
The chmod command is used to change permissions. To give the owner (u) read (r) and write (w) permission, and explicitly remove permissions from the group (g) and others (o):
Command (Symbolic):
chmod u=rw,g=,o= filename


Command (Octal):
chmod 600 filename


(Where 6 = read+write for owner, and 00 means no permissions for group or others).
